{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.vTwo_not_descent_measure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.vTwo_not_descent_measure","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L194-L216","doc":"**`v_[2]` is not a descent measure on any cone containing `witnessP`.**\n\nIn particular it is not one on `D∞`, which does contain `witnessP` (verified\nboth by construction as a backward orbit of the attractor and forward by\niteration). Instantiating `f` at the Skein-Collatz map, `target` at the\nattractor and `S` at `domainStable` refutes exactly the `hdesc` hypothesis of\n`reaches_cycle_of_descent_domainStable` for `μ = v_[2]`.\n\n**Scope (a).** This excludes `v_[2]`, not the descent route: some other `μ`\nmay still work. What survives as forward guidance is\n`descent_measure_pos_off_target` — any candidate must be strictly positive at\nevery non-attractor point of the cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessCP_pow_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessCP_pow_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L186-L190","doc":"**`v_[2](C(witnessP)) ≥ 7`** — exhibited by `C(P) = q⁻¹·(q+1)⁷`. So the step\ndoes not merely fail to descend, it climbs by seven. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.laurentTwoVal_witnessP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.laurentTwoVal_witnessP","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L182-L184","doc":"**`v_[2](witnessP) = 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP_qOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP_qOdd","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L175-L180","doc":"`witnessP` is `q`-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP_step","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L169-L173","doc":"The odd branch takes `witnessP` to `witnessCP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessCP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessCP","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L165-L167","doc":"Its Collatz image `C(P) = q⁻¹·(q+1)⁷`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witnessP","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L158-L163","doc":"The witness `P = q⁻¹·(q⁶+7q⁵+20q⁴+29q³+21q²+6q+1)`, an element of `D∞`\nverified in `computations/qcollatz_vtwo_domain_stable_probe.py` (it reaches\nthe attractor cycle in 7 steps). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.qunit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.qunit","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L154-L156","doc":"`q` is a unit in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`, with inverse `q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witness_qOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witness_qOdd","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L147-L152","doc":"**The witness is `q`-odd, generically**: `P + 1 = [2]_q · (Y·B)` with\n`B = X⁵+6X⁴+14X³+15X²+6X+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witness_odd_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.witness_odd_step","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L134-L145","doc":"**The witness Collatz step, generically.** With `X = q`, `Y = q⁻¹`,\n\n  P  = Y·(X⁶+7X⁵+20X⁴+29X³+21X²+6X+1),   C(P) = Y·(X+1)⁷,\n\nthe odd branch `[3]_q·P + 1 = [2]_q·C(P)` holds. (Cleared of `Y` this is the\ninteger identity `(X²+X+1)·A + X = (X+1)⁸`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.laurentTwoVal_qOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.laurentTwoVal_qOdd","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L119-L127","doc":"**`v_[2]` vanishes on every `q`-odd element.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.qOdd_not_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.qOdd_not_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**A `q`-odd element is not divisible by `[2]_q`.** If `[2]_q` divided both `P`\nand `P + 1` it would divide `1`, making it a unit — which it is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.not_descent_of_vanishes_off_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.not_descent_of_vanishes_off_target","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L96-L104","doc":"**Contrapositive — a measure that vanishes anywhere off the target cannot be\na descent measure.** This is the form used to refute a candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.descent_measure_pos_off_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzVTwoDinfRefutation.descent_measure_pos_off_target","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_dinf_refutation.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**Any `ℕ`-valued descent measure is strictly positive off the target.**\nImmediate, and the whole content of the refutation: `μ (f x) < μ x` cannot\nhold when `μ x = 0`, because `ℕ` has nothing below `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}